# Rosa, the chatty newsstand owner outside Dave's building.
# GameState is passed in by Room.start_dialogue(), so we can check items/flags.

~ start
if GameState.has_flag("tipped_off")
	Rosa: Still here? Go on, catch your plane. And keep an eye on that grey coat.
	=> END
if GameState.has_flag("met_rosa")
	Rosa: Back again, Dave? You know I charge for conversation after the third visit.
else
	Rosa: Dave! Just the man. Did you hear? The Kowalskis' parrot learned the doorbell. Nobody on the third floor has slept in a week.
	do GameState.set_flag("met_rosa")
=> menu

~ menu
- Any gossip, Rosa?
	Rosa: The baker's nephew is "in import-export" again. That means the police will be round by Thursday.
	Rosa: And somebody pushed a postcard under your door this morning. Foreign stamp. I didn't read it. Much.
	=> menu
- Seen anyone odd around here?
	Rosa: Only the gentleman behind me. He's been on the same page for ten minutes. Slow reader, or very dull newspaper.
	Dave: Or he isn't reading at all.
	=> menu
- Found this in the gutter. Mean anything to you? [if GameState.has_item("boarding_pass") /]
	=> show_pass
- See you, Rosa.
	Rosa: Don't be a stranger! Well. Any stranger than usual.
	=> END

~ show_pass
Dave: Found this boarding pass in the gutter. Mean anything to you?
Rosa: Aurora Air! My sister flew with them once. Never again - they charge you for the armrest.
Rosa: And that name, H. Grau... that's him! The grey coat by my stand. Bought a paper with a hundred-euro note. Who does that?
Rosa: A standby pass. Flies wherever, whenever - from the same airport you'd use, Dave. And he's been watching your door all morning.
Dave: Rosa, you'd have made a terrific spy.
Rosa: Who says I didn't?
do GameState.set_flag("tipped_off")
=> END
